      "problem": "What is the value of $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{t+3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+3) \\\\ \\sqrt{{t}^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}]$ at $t=-2?$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $t=-2$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-2) & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(-2)+3} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡((-2)+3) \\\\ \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡1 \\\\ \\sqrt{4-1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the value of $f(t)$ at $t=-2$ is the vector $[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].$",
